  <page_number>246</page_number>
  <running_head>Castigatio Paral.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">capitis sexti, his verbis: <i>Feramur ergo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>ad perfectionem non jacientes rursum fun-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>damentum refipiscentiae ab operibus mortuis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>&amp; fide in Deum, &amp;c.</i> Hortatio propo-</l>
    <l n="5">nitur axiomate discreto, cuius pars</l>
    <l n="6">consequens explicatur per membra,</l>
    <l n="7">posteriori colo v. 1. &amp; v. 2. integro.</l>
    <l n="8">Dum ostendit, in quibus fundamen-</l>
    <l n="9">tum religionis, quod supra rudem ser-</l>
    <l n="10">monem vocavit, &amp; in quo illi instituti</l>
    <l n="11">erant, consistat. Nempe in doctrina</l>
    <l n="12">1. refipiscentiae ab operibus mortuis,</l>
    <l n="13">2. fidei in Deum, 3. baptismi, 4.</l>
    <l n="14">manuum impositionis, 5. resurrectio-</l>
    <l n="15">nis mortuorum, &amp; 6. iudicii aeterni.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Hanc doctrinam semel suscepta m,</l>
    <l n="17">dicit, non saltem non deserendam sed</l>
    <l n="18">ab hac ad perfectionem tendendum</l>
    <l n="19">esse v. 1.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Id probat argumento ex hac ipsa</l>
    <l n="21">doctrina desumpto, sed mutatis phra-</l>
    <l n="22">sibus. Versiculo enim 1, &amp; 2. causas,</l>
    <l n="23">versiculo vero 4. &amp; 5. effecta tradit.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Dicit</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Running head and page number read as printed; "suscepta m" is a printed-line-end reading and may be "susceptam". Catchword absent.</notes>
</page>
